build/
out/
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.spv
CMakeUserPresets.json
package/

# The overnight loop's stop marker, created by hand to ask a running loop to finish.
STOP-LOOP

# A clip's built world, kept beside it so the next run does not rebuild it. Derived from the
# .clip file, hundreds of megabytes, and rebuilt automatically whenever the clip changes — so it
# is exactly the kind of thing that must never be committed.
*.clip.world
*.clip.world.part

renders/

# The game's own user folder. On Windows it lives under %LOCALAPPDATA%; off Windows there is no
# such place, so `local_app_data_dir` puts it beside the binary and a run from the repository root
# creates it there. The names inside are ignored below in their own right; this is the folder.
WorldShaper/

# How long each stage of a load took last run, so the next one can weight its bar by what
# things actually cost here. Per-machine, like the built-world cache beside it.
*.clip.load

# Agent worktrees, created under the repository so a subagent can build without touching this
# tree (CLAUDE.md, "Subagents"). Each one is a whole checkout with its own build directory, so
# committing them would put the repository inside itself.
.claude/worktrees/

# The clip viewer's baked clips. Derived from the .clip files by tools/bake_web.cpp, tens of
# megabytes of binary, and rebuilt by .github/workflows/pages.yml on every push that can change
# them. Committing them would put a second copy of every clip in the history, out of date the
# moment somebody edits a fragment.
web/data/
build-tools/
build-web/
